{
  "requirement": "The workspace `[evidence]` table MUST serialize EvidenceConfig. `allow` and\n`disallow` MUST be arrays of nonempty literal paths, each naming a file or a\ndirectory subtree. Relative paths MUST resolve from the selected `habeas.toml`\ndirectory; absolute paths MUST be supported. These paths are not glob patterns.\n\nFor authoring reads, a matching disallow MUST reject the path; otherwise a\nmatching allow MUST permit it; otherwise the default source-access rules MUST\napply. Explicit allow MUST override every default, including Git tracking,\nproject containment, generated-evidence exclusion, and automatic generated-output\nrules. Disallow MUST win even when an allow or generated-output rule also matches.\nBoth the requested path and its resolved symlink target MUST be checked for\ndisallow, so an allowed alias cannot expose a disallowed target.\n\nThe same explicit disallow rules and external-path exceptions MUST apply when\nresolving recorded evidence inputs, including ordinary validation and\n`add-input`. Validation MUST remain independent of Git index membership: it\nchecks the recorded inputs' existence and contents. Loading path policy MUST NOT\nresolve credentials or validate unused authoring settings.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "The behavior is implemented and tested well, but part of the implementation has no `{impl}` marker. That is a gap under the marking rule.\n\n**What is implemented and marked correctly**\n- `src/config.rs` `EvidenceConfig::validate` and `load_workspace_evidence` cover several obligations.\n  - Entries must be nonempty and contain no NUL.\n  - Unknown keys are rejected.\n  - Only the `[evidence]` table is decoded, so credentials are not resolved and unused authoring settings are not validated.\n- `PathPolicy::load` (`src/authoring/access.rs`) resolves relative rules against the `habeas.toml` directory. `Path::join` leaves absolute rules unchanged, so absolute paths are supported. Rules are matched as literal path prefixes, not globs, via `matches_rule`.\n- `check_disallow` runs before `allowed`.\n  - It checks both the requested location and its ancestors, plus the resolved symlink target. An allowed alias therefore cannot expose a disallowed target.\n  - `SourceAccess::path` checks disallow first, then explicit allow, and only then credentials, generated evidence, containment and Git tracking. Explicit allow therefore overrides every default.\n  - `omit_generated_evidence` makes disallow win over the generated-output rules.\n- `resolve_evidence_file` (reached through `check_project_file` → `OutlineCache::parse` for validation and `add-input`) applies the same disallow and external-path exceptions. It does not consult the Git index, so validation stays independent of Git membership.\n- `list_files`, `search`, `project_path`, `source_input` and the other tool functions are marked as consumers of the same policy.\n\n**Tests**\n- `access.rs` tests cover:\n  - allow overriding the defaults (generated output, `evidence/`, an external directory);\n  - disallow winning for a subtree and for a symlink alias;\n  - disallowed ancestors redirecting through symlinks;\n  - `..` after a symlink.\n- `tools.rs` tests cover list, search and read for allowed, external and disallowed paths, and Cargo output.\n- `tests/commands.rs` covers `status` and `add-input` with allow and disallow, and loading that skips unused authoring settings.\n- `tests/configuration.rs` and `tests/evidence_boundaries.rs` cover:\n  - rejected malformed entries (empty string, non-string, unknown field);\n  - validation of external inputs, including freshness and disallow;\n  - disallowed symlink ancestors;\n  - invalid workspace config;\n  - that unused authoring settings are not loaded.\n\n**Gap**\n- The requirement says \"The workspace `[evidence]` table MUST serialize EvidenceConfig\".\n  - `struct EvidenceConfig` (`src/config.rs` lines 46–53) is the code that does this. It defines the `allow` and `disallow` `Vec<PathBuf>` fields, `deny_unknown_fields`, and the serde serialize/deserialize behavior.\n  - The `evidence: Option<EvidenceConfig>` field on `WorkspaceConfig` and the `WorkspaceEvidenceConfig` struct that carries the loaded policy also have no reference.\n  - None of these carries an `{impl}` for `requirements.configuration.evidence_paths`. The `references` listing shows no site on them, and the struct source has no attached reference comment.\n  - `PathPolicy` (`src/authoring/access.rs` lines 9–14), which stores the resolved allow and disallow lists, is also unmarked.\n- These are not acknowledged by any `FIXME`, so the result is false, not a FIXME determination.\n- `tests/configuration.rs` and the `status` tests exercise parsing and validation but do not directly test serialization of the `[evidence]` table. The \"MUST serialize EvidenceConfig\" obligation is therefore both unmarked in the implementation and only indirectly verified.",
  "inputs": [
